Created the generic recovery workflow:

- [recover-missing-taxonids.sh](./scripts/recover-missing-taxonids.sh)
- [recover-missing-taxonids-from-evidence.sql](./Databases/scripts/recover-missing-taxonids-from-evidence.sql)

Usage after the `tlkptaxon` repair:

```bash
scripts/recover-missing-taxonids.sh TARGET_DATABASE taxonfix
```

The script:

- Exports latest conflict-free evidence from `taxonfix`.
- Updates only null or blank `tblelement.taxonid` values.
- Normalizes `legacy-` evidence IDs.
- Requires candidates to exist in repaired `tlkptaxon`.
- Runs the target update transactionally.
- Reports unresolved evidence without applying it.
- Refuses to run while legacy taxa or orphaned links remain.

Full Christy clone testing recovered 731 values:

```text
